            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy Skaggs Tranter"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is always a hit with my family and friends. I make it without the MSG and onion salt. I always double this recipe, because it's never enough, use 2 green onions, 1 1/2 Tblsp. Worchesteshire sauce and the \"family size\" pack of dried beef. Reserve a little of the beef to roll the ball in...it makes a pretty presentation.\r\n\r\nGreat with wheat crackers!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Polly A Long"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been using this recipe for over 20 years. Mine is a little different. I do not use the MSG why would you? I use 1 tsp. garlic salt and use a small minced onion and put 3 tablespoons of sour cream into the mixture. Then I cut little squares of dried beef and cover the outside to make it prettier.",
            "datePublished": "2014-10-15T08:19:50.407Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brenda Walker Watkins"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Have made this many times for pot luck and parties. The first time I made it I didn't rinse the dried beef before I chopped it and it was way too salty. Now I rinse the beef before I chop to a fine consistancy. I get requests to bring this cheese ball and a pineapple ball too.",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-30T18:23:07.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MamaMary"
            },
            "reviewBody": "RINSE THE BEEF! If you use the real DRIED BEEF, rather than the cheaper smoked beef, it is very salty. I ruined a double batch by not rinsing. It was just to terribly salty. Headed back to store for more beef and rinsed it. Ahhh, success. I don't use MSG. I did pick up some horseradish the 2nd trip to the grocery store and added a bit. Emmm, good. The green onions are a must. They add nice color and a bit of sweetness. I use all of the onion, white and green. This is so addictive. I've had before but never made. At work there was a carry-in for Easter and I could have sat down with a spoon and consumed the whole thing. I asked for the basic receipe, stopped at the store and then checked out allrecipes.com. This is a winner!",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-07T06:11:24.487Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alana Koepfer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Using the amount of dried beef in the recipe was way too much and too salty. Substituting a 2oz package of Buddig beef was perfect and not at all too salty.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-01T15:59:24.507Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lorrie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a hit at all my get togethers. I leave out the MSG, and I too, rinse the beef before chopping it. Instead of making a \"ball\" out of it, I shape it into a small loaf. Serve with wheat thins, because they aren't very salty.",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-26T15:35:16.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clayzzle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This could've been so good if I'd listened to other reviewers and rinsed the salt off the dried beef! But no, alas, I did not listen and served a salty ball of salt to my guests. And I didn't happen to have MSG on hand, shocking I know, so didn't add it. Also, I used onion powder in place of onion salt. I will make this again, because the base flavor was yummy, but I will definitely rinse the beef. And add a little dijon mustard. If not for the crazy saltiness, I would've given this 5 stars.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-21T15:10:41.577Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa Powers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this variation for over 30 years, sometimes adding green olives, once in awhile substituting different kinds of meat, like sliced buddig brand beef, or ham, when they were sold out of dried Armour beef in a jar . It is always loved and eaten by my family, with none left over.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-01T03:23:04.004Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Faith N"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was amazing. My sister had made it for me a few times but I had no idea on measurements until I found this on AR. I didn't use the monosodium glutamate or onion salt but it still tasted just like hers (which included those.) Added another 1/2 onion just because I love their flavor. I also took the advice of someone else on here and washed the salt off the dried beef before chopping it up. My 4 and 1 year olds also loved this - will make it again!",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-29T12:00:58.563Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "smileyashmommy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I always take this cheese ball to our annual Christmas party and every year it's the first thing gone! I do make a few minor changes. I don't use the MSG and instead of onion salt I use garlic salt. After I make the ball I place it in plastic wrap and form it into a ball then let it chill in the fridge. After a few hours I pull it out and roll it in a bowl of sliced almonds for a pretty and delicious presentation. It's a hit!",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-13T11:55:45.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carol Michels"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was good, and I'll make it again. However, even with the substitution of onion powder for the onion salt, it was crazy-salty. Next time, I'll soak the beef in water or milk to leach out some of the salt first. And I'll cut the onion powder in half. I prefer the taste of the fresh green onions. Good foundation recipe. :)",
            "datePublished": "2010-11-07T06:08:26.757Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chela421"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Add grenadine to this type of cheese ball...just enough to make it a light pink!! Sooo good!",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-10T00:22:45.877Z"
